faqs:
  - q: How does your online ordering system compare to DoorDash or UberEats?
    a: DoorDash and UberEats take 15-30% of every order. Our system gives you your own branded online ordering through your website with zero commission fees. Payments are integrated directly into the platform — no separate processor needed. Customers order directly from you for pickup or delivery. You keep the customer relationship, their data, and the vast majority of the revenue. Some customers will still use delivery apps, but giving them an alternative means more profit on every direct order.
  - q: Can I update my menu myself or do I need to contact you every time?
    a: You can update your menu instantly through a simple dashboard. Change prices, add specials, mark items as sold out, update descriptions and photos — all in seconds from your phone or computer. No waiting on a web developer. No extra fees. Seasonal menus, daily specials, and happy hour pricing are all easy to manage yourself.
  - q: How much can I actually save by consolidating tools?
    a: Most restaurants pay for a website, online ordering system, POS software, email marketing, and loyalty programs separately — $500-$1,500/month in disconnected tools. GullStack consolidates everything into one platform with integrated payments, saving $6,000-$18,000/year in subscription fees. Add your own commission-free online ordering instead of DoorDash's 15-30% cut, and the total savings grow even more.
  - q: Do you help with Google Business Profile and local search?
    a: Yes. For restaurants, Google Business Profile is one of the most important marketing channels. We optimize your profile with accurate hours, menus, photos, and category selections. We also help you manage and respond to reviews, post updates about specials and events, and ensure your information is consistent across all online directories. When someone searches for restaurants near me or a specific cuisine type in your area, we make sure you show up.
  - q: Can I still use delivery apps alongside your ordering system?
    a: Absolutely. We do not ask you to stop using delivery apps. They provide exposure and convenience that some customers prefer. Our approach is to give you an additional channel — your own website ordering — that captures orders at a fraction of the cost. Many restaurants find that once they promote their direct ordering option, a significant portion of delivery app customers switch over, especially with small incentives like free delivery or loyalty points.
